.TH FPTAD 1 "2026-11-27" "fprint-tpm-authenticator 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
fptad \- FIDO2 security key backed by a fingerprint reader and TPM 2.0
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fptad
[\fB\-\-socket\fR \fIpath\fR | \fB\-\-fd\fR \fIn\fR]
[\fB\-\-state\-dir\fR \fIdir\fR] [\fB\-\-tcti\fR \fIconf\fR]
.br
.B fptad \-\-check
[\fB\-\-tcti\fR \fIconf\fR]
.br
.BR "fptad \-\-version" " | " \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
The per-user daemon of a virtual CTAP2 security key. It is normally started by
the systemd user unit
.B fptad.service
and connects to
.BR fpta\-broker ,
which owns the virtual HID device. Every registration and sign-in is confirmed
through
.BR fprintd (1).
Signing keys are created by and never leave the TPM.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-check
Open the TPM, create the primary key, report the result and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-socket " path"
Broker socket. Default /run/fpta-broker.sock.
.TP
.BI \-\-fd " n"
Use an inherited SOCK_SEQPACKET descriptor.
.TP
.BI \-\-state\-dir " dir"
Default $XDG_DATA_HOME/fpta or ~/.local/share/fpta.
.TP
.BI \-\-tcti " conf"
TPM transport. Default device:/dev/tpmrm0.
.SH FILES
The state directory holds a secret that authenticates credential IDs, the
signature counter and discoverable credentials. Deleting it destroys every
passkey and security-key registration made with this authenticator.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fprintd (1),
.BR fido2\-token (1)
